---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
import dmd from '../assets/screens/dmd-5620.png';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Screenshots — ipnx"
  description="The emulated DMD 5620 terminal running Research Unix Eighth Edition on a Mac."
  eyebrow="Plates"
  heading="Screenshots"
  intro="Photographed off a working machine, not mocked up."
>
  <div class="py-8">
    <figure>
      <Image
        src={dmd}
        alt="The ipnx DMD 5620 window: green phosphor text on black showing a login as christie, the welcome message, a fortune, and the output of ipnxfetch reporting ipnx Edition 8 Release 1.0 on an emulated VAX-11/780 with 8128 KiB of memory."
        widths={[720, 1080, 1440]}
        sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 900px"
        loading="eager"
        class="w-full border border-rule shadow-card"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] font-sans text-[14px] text-muted">
        The DMD 5620 at a shell. The window is locked to the terminal's own 800×1024 portrait
        shape; the toolbar carries the mouse-button hints, the pointer grab and a BREAK key,
        because a real 5620 had one and Research Unix expects it.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[68ch] border-t border-rule pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-[24px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em]">More to come</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] text-body">
        <code class="bg-chip px-1 font-mono text-[0.86em]">mux</code> with a layer swept open, and
        <code class="bg-chip px-1 font-mono text-[0.86em]">jim</code> editing inside it, are the
        two pictures this page most wants and does not yet have — both need a mouse in a human
        hand, and a screenshot of them faked from anything else would be worth nothing. They will
        appear here once taken properly.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] text-body">
        In the meantime, <a
          href={href('/manual/mux-and-layers')}
          class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emphasis">the manual</a
        > describes exactly what to do, and it takes about a minute on your own machine.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
